## Detecting File Types from Extensions

A filename like `"vacation.jpg"` has an extension at the end. By checking that extension, you can classify the file into a type.

### The FileType Enum

```xiom
enum FileType {
  Image(ext: Str),
  Document(ext: Str),
  Video(ext: Str),
  Unknown,
}
```

Each known type carries the actual extension so you can display it.

### The Detection Function

Use a series of `if` checks to classify by extension:

```xiom
fn detect(filename: Str) -> FileType {
  let len = string.str_len(filename);
  if len < 4 {
    return FileType.Unknown;
  }
  let last3 = /* last 3 characters */;
  if last3 == "jpg" || last3 == "png" || last3 == "gif" {
    return FileType.Image(last3);
  }
  if last3 == "pdf" || last3 == "txt" || last3 == "doc" {
    return FileType.Document(last3);
  }
  if last3 == "mp4" || last3 == "avi" || last3 == "mov" {
    return FileType.Video(last3);
  }
  return FileType.Unknown;
}
```

### Using the Detector

```xiom
let f1 = detect("photo.jpg");   // Image("jpg")
let f2 = detect("report.pdf");  // Document("pdf")
let f3 = detect("movie.mp4");   // Video("mp4")
let f4 = detect("README");      // Unknown
```

### Describing Detected Types

```xiom
fn describe_type(ft: FileType) -> Str {
  match ft {
    Image(ext) => { return "Image (." + ext + ")"; }
    Document(ext) => { return "Document (." + ext + ")"; }
    Video(ext) => { return "Video (." + ext + ")"; }
    Unknown => { return "Unknown file type"; }
  }
}
```

